# Do not improvise. Do only what was asked.

## Shipped baseline (do not abandon)

- **Shipped feature tip the user expects:** PR #15 — `cursor/themes-trips-shopping-c30d` @ `c92258a` (themes, real itineraries, shopping mode), including brand animations and prior Home/Tasks/Rewards/shared-device work on that lineage.
- Do **not** check out, merge into, or “continue” on `cursor/choremaxx-make-v7-c30d` (or other divergent Make-only branches) unless the user **explicitly** names that branch or asks for a Make sync/port.
- Parallel agent branches are not disposable. Never replace welcome/sign-in/Home/Tasks polish with a static Make port without an explicit merge/restore request.

## Scope lock

When the user asks only to **start the terminal / Metro / Expo tunnel / QR**:

1. Start (or restart) `npm run start:tunnel` on the **current checked-out commit**.
2. Report the `exp://…` URL.
3. **Stop.** Do not switch branches, sync Figma, restore animations, merge PRs, “fix” Make v7, or otherwise change code.

Same rule for any narrow ask: do that task only. Do not “helpfully” port designs, unify branches, or rewrite auth/onboarding.

## Forbidden without an explicit ask

- Figma Make sync / `get_design_context` / porting Make source into Expo
